  "disposition": "implementation_updated",
  "summary": "Reject an infinite-plane triangle backface fallback when feature clipping finds no contact and its projected point lies outside the finite triangle.",
  "regressions": [
    "A live mesh/polyhedron pair produced a false contact more than 0.6 units outside its triangle with penetration depth -0.60767436. The native regression rejects that contact while retaining its neighboring triangle's valid speculative contact.",
    "The mirrored TileLang path uses the existing triangle projection and the same FLT_EPS*100 bound; invalid fallback output returns the native empty manifold."
  ],
  "differences": [
    "This fixes reference geometry and the translation together; it is not a tolerance relaxation or a fabricated witness.",
    "Native edge-clipping secondary-witness approximation remains a separate recorded limitation."
  ],
